    {
      "id": "25595974",
      "title": "A Closer Look at the \"useState\" Hook",
      "sourceHash": "bd124f7aa740c7e07a057081509095b401583493cae98d41475426fc640109c8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.3,
          "end": 4.033,
          "en": "Tutor: So now we learned about State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.033,
          "end": 6.4,
          "en": "And State as you can probably tell by now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.4,
          "end": 8.966,
          "en": "is a key concept in React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.966,
          "end": 10.733,
          "en": "Now, there are a couple of things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.733,
          "end": 12.933,
          "en": "I wanna clarify about useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.933,
          "end": 16.633,
          "en": "and about why we use a const here, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.633,
          "end": 19.3,
          "en": "Now, first let's start with one important thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.3,
          "end": 21.5,
          "en": "which I did mention in the last lecture already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.5,
          "end": 25.166,
          "en": "UseState registers some State,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.166,
          "end": 27.633,
          "en": "so some value as a State",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.633,
          "end": 30.933,
          "en": "for the component in which it is being called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.933,
          "end": 34.066,
          "en": "And I wanna be even more precise here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.066,
          "end": 38.433,
          "en": "It registers it for a specific component instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.433,
          "end": 40.566,
          "en": "For example, ExpenseItem here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.566,
          "end": 43.433,
          "en": "is being used four times, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.433,
          "end": 47.966,
          "en": "And Expenses.js we have four ExpenseItems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.966,
          "end": 52.233,
          "en": "Now, every item receives its own separate State",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.233,
          "end": 55.3,
          "en": "which is detached from the other States.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.3,
          "end": 55.766,
          "en": "which is detached from the other States.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.766,
          "end": 58.466,
          "en": "We have one ExpenseItem definition here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.466,
          "end": 62.4,
          "en": "but then this function is basically called four times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 65.3,
          "en": "when we create four ExpenseItems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.3,
          "end": 65.733,
          "en": "when we create four ExpenseItems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.733,
          "end": 70.333,
          "en": "And every time it's called, a new separate State is created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.333,
          "end": 71.966,
          "en": "of course in the same way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.966,
          "end": 76,
          "en": "but managed independently by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76,
          "end": 76.43299999999999,
          "en": "but managed independently by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.43299999999999,
          "end": 78.333,
          "en": "So if we change the title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.333,
          "end": 82.5,
          "en": "in the first ExpenseItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.5,
          "end": 84.46600000000001,
          "en": "the other ones are not affected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.46600000000001,
          "end": 86.9,
          "en": "because they have their own State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 86.9,
          "end": 88.1,
          "en": "That's really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.1,
          "end": 92.43299999999999,
          "en": "It's on a per component instance basis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 92.43299999999999,
          "end": 92.7,
          "en": "It's on a per component instance basis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.7,
          "end": 94.63300000000001,
          "en": "So we have separate States,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 94.63300000000001,
          "end": 98.566,
          "en": "even if we create a component more than once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.566,
          "end": 98.666,
          "en": "even if we create a component more than once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 98.666,
          "end": 100.566,
          "en": "And that's of course crucial",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 100.566,
          "end": 103.76599999999999,
          "en": "because it would be a rather undesired behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.76599999999999,
          "end": 106.5,
          "en": "if we change something in one item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 106.5,
          "end": 109.63300000000001,
          "en": "and all the other items are updated as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 109.63300000000001,
          "end": 113.76599999999999,
          "en": "So that's a good thing to have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.76599999999999,
          "end": 116.9,
          "en": "Now, in addition, whenever State changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.9,
          "end": 119.1,
          "en": "because we click a button in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 119.1,
          "end": 121.433,
          "en": "it's only this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 121.433,
          "end": 123.9,
          "en": "and only that specific instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 123.9,
          "end": 126.1,
          "en": "where this component is being used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.1,
          "end": 129.466,
          "en": "where React will re-evaluate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 129.466,
          "end": 129.966,
          "en": "where React will re-evaluate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 129.966,
          "end": 132.166,
          "en": "And you can tell that this is the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 132.166,
          "end": 135.566,
          "en": "if you add a number of console.log here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 135.566,
          "end": 137.6,
          "en": "in the component, function itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 137.6,
          "end": 138.03300000000002,
          "en": "in the component, function itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 138.03300000000002,
          "end": 145.066,
          "en": "where you say ExpenseItem evaluated by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 145.066,
          "end": 147.666,
          "en": "This will be called whenever the ExpenseItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 147.666,
          "end": 151.266,
          "en": "component function is being executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 151.266,
          "end": 151.8,
          "en": "component function is being executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 151.8,
          "end": 156.266,
          "en": "And therefore if I reload, we see it's called four times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 156.266,
          "end": 156.833,
          "en": "And therefore if I reload, we see it's called four times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 156.833,
          "end": 158.03300000000002,
          "en": "which makes a lot of sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 158.03300000000002,
          "end": 162.53300000000002,
          "en": "because we're using ExpenseItem four times in expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 162.53300000000002,
          "end": 162.666,
          "en": "because we're using ExpenseItem four times in expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 162.666,
          "end": 164.766,
          "en": "So four separate instances",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 164.766,
          "end": 168.466,
          "en": "of this component are being created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 168.466,
          "end": 170.733,
          "en": "But if I now click on change title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 170.733,
          "end": 172.933,
          "en": "in one of the ExpenseItems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 172.933,
          "end": 175.6,
          "en": "we see it's only printed once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 175.6,
          "end": 176.966,
          "en": "Which is basically happening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 176.966,
          "end": 179.133,
          "en": "because of what I just explained.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 179.133,
          "end": 182.433,
          "en": "Only that specific instance is being updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 182.433,
          "end": 184.833,
          "en": "and therefore for being re-evaluated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 184.833,
          "end": 184.933,
          "en": "and therefore for being re-evaluated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 184.933,
          "end": 188,
          "en": "and the other instances are not affected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 188,
          "end": 190.433,
          "en": "by that State change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 190.433,
          "end": 192.233,
          "en": "And that's important to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 192.233,
          "end": 194.666,
          "en": "that State really is separated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 194.666,
          "end": 198.7,
          "en": "on a per component instance basis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 198.7,
          "end": 201.5,
          "en": "Now there's one other thing which could be confusing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 201.5,
          "end": 204.633,
          "en": "And that's the fact that I'm using const here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 204.633,
          "end": 206.766,
          "en": "Why am I using const here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 206.766,
          "end": 211.133,
          "en": "when we do eventually assign a new value?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 211.133,
          "end": 212.633,
          "en": "Well, keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 212.633,
          "end": 215.733,
          "en": "that we're not assigning a value with the equal sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 215.733,
          "end": 217.433,
          "en": "That would indeed fail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 217.433,
          "end": 220.266,
          "en": "but that is not how we assign a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 220.266,
          "end": 222.166,
          "en": "when we update a State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 222.166,
          "end": 222.5,
          "en": "when we update a State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 222.5,
          "end": 225.53300000000002,
          "en": "Instead we call this State updating function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 225.53300000000002,
          "end": 229.833,
          "en": "and the concrete value is simply managed somewhere else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 229.833,
          "end": 231.03300000000002,
          "en": "by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 231.03300000000002,
          "end": 234.03300000000002,
          "en": "By calling useState we tell React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 234.03300000000002,
          "end": 236.6,
          "en": "that it should manage some value for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 236.6,
          "end": 240.633,
          "en": "We never see that variable itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 240.633,
          "end": 243.3,
          "en": "So therefore, we just call a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 243.3,
          "end": 243.366,
          "en": "So therefore, we just call a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 243.366,
          "end": 246.2,
          "en": "and we never assign a new value to title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 246.2,
          "end": 248.7,
          "en": "with the equal operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 248.7,
          "end": 248.833,
          "en": "with the equal operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 248.833,
          "end": 252.766,
          "en": "And therefore, using a const is absolutely fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 252.766,
          "end": 256.1,
          "en": "How do we get the latest title value then though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 256.1,
          "end": 258.433,
          "en": "Well, keep in mind that the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 258.433,
          "end": 261.33299999999997,
          "en": "is re-executed when the State is updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 261.33299999999997,
          "end": 261.4,
          "en": "is re-executed when the State is updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 261.4,
          "end": 263.766,
          "en": "And therefore, of course, this line of code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 263.766,
          "end": 266.9,
          "en": "line nine, also is executed again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 266.9,
          "end": 270.8,
          "en": "whenever the component function is executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 270.8,
          "end": 273.233,
          "en": "So if we called setTitle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 273.233,
          "end": 275.266,
          "en": "and we assign a new title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 275.266,
          "end": 278.5,
          "en": "that leads to this component being called again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 278.5,
          "end": 278.733,
          "en": "that leads to this component being called again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 278.733,
          "end": 283.733,
          "en": "and therefore, this new title, this updated title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 283.733,
          "end": 286.533,
          "en": "is fetched from React, which manages the State for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 286.533,
          "end": 288.9,
          "en": "is fetched from React, which manages the State for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 288.9,
          "end": 290.533,
          "en": "Basically we go to React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 290.533,
          "end": 294.5,
          "en": "and say, \"Hey please give me that latest title State",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 294.5,
          "end": 297,
          "en": "which I told you to manage for me.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 297,
          "end": 300.866,
          "en": "And React provides us this latest State in this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 300.866,
          "end": 304.066,
          "en": "which useState always returns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 304.066,
          "end": 304.6,
          "en": "which useState always returns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 304.6,
          "end": 307.5,
          "en": "So we always get a brand new snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 307.5,
          "end": 312,
          "en": "of that State when this component function re-executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 312,
          "end": 315.8,
          "en": "That's how this works under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 315.8,
          "end": 318.5,
          "en": "Now you might be wondering if that doesn't mean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 318.5,
          "end": 321.9,
          "en": "that we always overwrite any State changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 321.9,
          "end": 324.4,
          "en": "with props.title again, here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 324.4,
          "end": 324.6,
          "en": "with props.title again, here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 324.6,
          "end": 328.133,
          "en": "And here, the special thing is that React keeps track",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 328.133,
          "end": 331.866,
          "en": "of when we call useState in a given component instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 331.866,
          "end": 333.83299999999997,
          "en": "for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 333.83299999999997,
          "end": 336.633,
          "en": "And when we call it for the first time ever,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 336.633,
          "end": 339.6,
          "en": "it'll take that argument as an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 339.6,
          "end": 339.83299999999997,
          "en": "it'll take that argument as an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 339.83299999999997,
          "end": 342.9,
          "en": "But if a component is then re-executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 342.9,
          "end": 345.666,
          "en": "because of such a State change, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 345.666,
          "end": 349.266,
          "en": "React will not reinitialize the State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
